8. Assign a deterministic calculation task.
9. Verify the Child was created by the application.
10. Verify task creation and delivery.
11. Verify the Extension inserted the Child prompt.
12. Verify the Extension actually submitted the prompt.
13. Observe the Child execution passively.
14. Verify the Child completed through supported tools.
15. Verify result delivery to the Parent.
16. Verify required acknowledgement.
17. Confirm there were no duplicate children, tasks, or completions.
18. Clean up test-owned resources.
19. Record the outcome and evidence.

### Pass conditions

A test passes only if the entire documented lifecycle is correct.

The result must be supported by actual runtime state and application evidence, not merely ChatGPT's final response.

