# 10. GENERAL TEST EXECUTION ALGORITHM

Execute every scenario through a standardized lifecycle.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Select Highest-Priority Test"]
    B["Verify Preconditions"]
    C["Prepare Isolated Test State"]
    D["Execute via Authorized Path"]
    E["Monitor MCP, Browser and State"]
    F{"Expected Behavior Verified?"}
    G["Save PASS Evidence"]
    H["Capture Failure Evidence"]
    I["Determine First Incorrect State"]
    J["Delegate Targeted Opus Analysis"]
    K["Fable Validates Root Cause"]
    L["Implement Fix + Regression Test"]
    M["Rebuild / Restart Affected Components"]
    N["Rerun Failed Test"]
    O["Run Related Regression"]
    P["Update Coverage and Next Test"]

    A --> B --> C --> D --> E --> F
    F -- Yes --> G --> P
    F -- No --> H --> I --> J --> K --> L --> M --> N --> E
    N -.-> O
    O --> P --> A
```

All retry and investigation loops must be bounded.

### Testing stages

**Stage 1 — Smoke**

One Parent, one Child, one deterministic task.

**Stage 2 — Sequential workflows**

Repeated task assignment, completion, and result delivery.

**Stage 3 — Concurrency**

Multiple children, multiple independent parents, simultaneous events.

**Stage 4 — Nested delegation**

Parent → Child → Grandchild and deeper supported delegation.

**Stage 5 — Recovery**

Proxy, extension, browser, and network disruptions.

**Stage 6 — Security and isolation**

Ownership enforcement, credential validation, replay protection.

**Stage 7 — Stress and endurance**

Queue pressure, concurrency, memory/resource stability.

**Stage 8 — Full regression**

Repeat critical scenarios under clean conditions.

