4. Child prompt delivery uses Chat Orchestrator exclusively.
5. Parent/Child ownership and authorization are correct.
6. Task results are not silently lost within tested workloads.
7. Duplicate operations do not produce unintended side effects.
8. Session/incarnation handling passes recovery tests.
9. FIFO and acknowledgement behavior meet documented guarantees.
10. Proxy/extension/browser recovery scenarios pass.
11. Critical security checks pass.
12. Relevant regression tests pass after fixes.
13. Multiple clean E2E regression runs pass without manual intervention.
14. Configured stress and endurance profiles meet measured acceptance thresholds.
15. No confirmed sustained resource leak remains.
16. Installation/startup and recovery workflows are sufficiently automated.
17. Test artifacts provide trustworthy evidence of results.

### Recommended minimum exit verification

After resolving release blockers:

- Three consecutive clean critical E2E regression runs.
- Full completion of the prioritized P0/P1 scenario matrix.
- Zero confirmed lost task results in the defined stress profile.
- Zero unauthorized cross-agent operations.
- Zero externally injected Child/Grandchild prompts.
- No unresolved critical deadlock or state corruption.
- A completed documented endurance profile without sustained resource leakage.

Define performance and workload thresholds using actual system limits.

Do not claim mathematical proof of zero bugs or exhaustive coverage of every possible real-world event.

